@* The image this build produced, and the base image behind it (TFND-134).

   A base image is usually the single largest source of inherited CVEs in a
   deployed artefact, and unlike a package it is one line in a Dockerfile — the
   highest leverage per fix available.

   The card leads with the BASE, not with the artefact. The artefact's own
   identity is on every other screen; the base image is the thing nothing else
   here can tell you. *@

<Card Padded="false">
    <div class="card-body">
        <h2>Container image</h2>
        <p class="field__help">
            What this build produced, and what it was built on. A base image is
            usually the largest single source of inherited CVEs — and the
            cheapest to change.
        </p>
    </div>

    @if (Images.Count == 0)
    {
        <div class="card-body">
            <div class="row">
                <Chip Label="NOT INSPECTED" Tone="var(--color-high)" Style="Chip.ChipStyle.Outlined" />
                <span class="muted">No container image was inspected on this build.</span>
            </div>
            @* Same rule as every scan receipt: an absent measurement is not a
               clean one. The gate reads Unknown rather than Pass, and this
               says why in the place somebody would fix it. *@
            <p class="field__help">
                That is not "no container" — it is that nobody looked. Add an image inspect to the
                pipeline (<code class="mono">Tamp.Trivy</code>'s <code class="mono">InspectImage</code>)
                and post it to <code class="mono">/ingest/container-image</code>.
            </p>
        </div>
    }
    else
    {
        <ScrollBox Label="Container images">
            <table class="table table--rows">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Image</th><th>Base image</th>
                        <th class="align-end">Base age at build</th><th>OS</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    @foreach (var image in Images)
                    {
                        <tr>
                            <td>
                                <div class="mono">@image.Reference</div>
                                @if (image.CreatedAt is { } built)
                                {
                                    <div class="field__help">built @built.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd")</div>
                                }
                            </td>
                            <td>
                                @if (image.BaseImageReference is { Length: > 0 } baseRef)
                                {
                                    <span class="mono">@baseRef</span>
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    @* The common case, and the message has to be
                                       actionable rather than apologetic: the OCI
                                       annotation is usually absent, and the fix is
                                       one string in the build script. *@
                                    <span class="muted">not identified</span>
                                    <div class="field__help">
                                        Most images do not carry the OCI annotation that names their
                                        base. Pass <code class="mono">baseImageReference</code> from
                                        your build — it is the string already in your
                                        <code class="mono">FROM</code> line.
                                    </div>
                                }
                            </td>
                            <td class="num align-end">
                                @if (image.BaseImageAgeInDays is { } age)
                                {
                                    <span style="@(age > 365 ? "color: var(--color-critical)"
                                                 : age > 180 ? "color: var(--color-high)" : null)">
                                        @age days
                                    </span>
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    <span class="muted">—</span>
                                }
                            </td>
                            <td>
                                @if (image.OsFamily is { Length: > 0 })
                                {
                                    <span class="mono">@image.OsFamily @image.OsVersion</span>
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    <span class="muted">—</span>
                                }
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                    }
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </ScrollBox>

        <div class="card-body">
            <p class="field__help">
                @* Stated once, plainly, because a number that silently means
                   something else is worse than no number. *@
                Age is measured at the <strong>build</strong>, not against today — so it does not
                drift upward every time this page is opened. "The base image was 400 days old when
                we shipped this" is a fact about the release.
            </p>
        </div>
    }
</Card>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public IReadOnlyList<ContainerImageRow> Images { get; set; } = [];
}
